+
+**Strengths and Limitations:**
+*   **Strengths:** Provides intuitive volume-centric navigation (zooming towards the clicked point). Simple to implement.
+*   **Limitations:** The specific order of transformations (position, zoom, rotation, centre, scale) is non-standard and may require careful understanding to debug. The light direction update logic in the source uses axis names that conflict with standard rotation matrix names (rotX around Y axis), which could lead to implementation errors if not carefully followed.
+
+**When to Use:**
+Use when implementing a volume renderer that requires intuitive zooming towards specific regions of interest within the volume.
+
+**When Not to Use:**
+Not suitable for general-purpose 3D scene navigation where standard camera models (like Arcball or Look-at) are preferred.
